# AWS CloudFront
AWS CloudFront is a Content Delivery Network (CDN) service that delivers your website, videos, images, APIs, and other content faster by storing copies of the content in Edge Locations (servers located around the world).

> Simple Explanation:
Imagine your website is hosted in Mumbai.
A user from Delhi requests your website.
A user from London also requests your website.

Without CloudFront:
Every request goes all the way to the server in Mumbai.
Users who are far away experience higher latency (slower loading).

With CloudFront:
CloudFront stores a cached copy of your website at nearby Edge Locations.
The Delhi user gets the content from a nearby Indian edge location.
The London user gets it from a nearby European edge location.
> Key Points (Interview)
CloudFront = AWS CDN service
Purpose: Faster content delivery
Works by: Caching content at Edge Locations
Origin can be: S3 Bucket, EC2, Application Load Balancer (ALB), or any web server
Benefits:
Faster website loading
Lower latency
Reduced load on the origin server

>Q. Why do we use CloudFront?
Answer:
We use AWS CloudFront to make websites and applications faster by caching content at Edge Locations near users. It reduces latency, decreases the load on the origin server, and improves the user experience.



# CDN = Content Delivery Network

Simple words mein: CDN ek network of servers hai jo website ka content user ke nearest server se deliver karta hai, jisse website fast load hoti hai.
1. CDN kya karta hai?
Suppose tumhari website ka main server Mumbai mein hai aur user Delhi mein hai.
Without CDN:
User Delhi
    ↓
Mumbai Server
    ↓
Website Content
Distance zyada → response comparatively slow.
With CDN:
                 ┌── Delhi CDN ──→ User
                 │
Main Server ──→ CDN Network
                 │
                 └── Mumbai CDN
User ko content nearest CDN server se mil sakta hai.
2. CDN mein kya store hota hai?
CDN commonly static content ko cache karta hai:
🖼️ Images
🎨 CSS files
📜 JavaScript files
🎥 Videos

> CDN ke Benefits
1. Faster Website
User ko nearest location se content milta hai.
2. Lower Latency
Request ko long distance travel nahi karna padta.
3. Reduced Server Load
Origin server ko har request handle nahi karni padti.
4. Better Scalability
Millions of users ko content serve karna easier hota hai.
5. Availability
Multiple edge locations hone ke karan service more resilient ho sakti hai.


> ☁️ AWS mein CDN
AWS ka CDN service hai:
Amazon CloudFront
Typical architecture:
              ┌── Edge Location ── User
              │
User → CloudFront
              │
              └── Origin
                    ↓
               S3 / EC2 / ALB
Example:
React Website
     ↓
   S3 Bucket
     ↓
CloudFront
     ↓
Users Worldwide
Yahan S3 origin ho sakta hai aur CloudFront CDN ki tarah kaam karta hai.